Z||000000||Philphine||10-12-2001||10:17 AM||||<BR>i've been playing with putting a changer in the passenger 4x10 spot and it looks like sony has the smallest trunk style 6disc changer. i was told once that since they came from the home market, their head units weren't very durable in cars. they over heat easy or something. <P>just need some user opinions 'cause i've never had any sony car gear. thanks for any help.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-12-2001||10:30 AM||||Well, I don't know about the trunk style 6 disc unit.  But I've got an older style Sony 10-disc changer that I've had for at least 5 years.  I'm running a Sony Tape Deck/Changer Control.  It works great!  I don't even have it hard mounted- just propped up (at an angle) behind the passenger seat and firewall. So it bounces around some, but still very rarely skips.  And quality wise- I'd buy another sony component any day.<P>Oh yeah, and the 10 disc cartridge can be swapped between my home player- and my car.  It's exactly the same piece.<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-12-2001||06:43 PM||||I've got a Sony CD head unit in my car.  If it ever wears out (or they come up with something new and improved), I'll buy Sony again.  I love mine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||10-12-2001||08:43 PM||||I've got a Sony 10 stacker I just took out of my MR2 that I might be coaxed into selling. It works great and is 5 years old. I just replaced the MR2s stereo with over $2500 worth of Pioneer and Clarion gear so I don't really need it. It kicks ass now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||10-12-2001||11:14 PM||||a tens too much. i made the rounds and tried an alpine, a panasonic 8disc (smaller than the alpine 6disc), and the new sony six. the sony's gonna fit. mounting it stable will be a project but i'm gonna go with it.<P>by the way, i think the other two would fit too but with more trimming and probaly taking out the dash to get at it better. i may have to take it out with the sony too.<P>thanks for the replies.||||reg||1
